WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.589
The SCP Foundation is no stranger to containing
dangerous entities capable of taking lives

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:07.150
without discretion.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:12.260
But some of those entities aren’t just mindless
monsters, they’re people, with feelings

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:19.770
and desires, stuck in an unfortunate circumstance,
granted unnatural abilities by fate or chance.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:24.320
For a lot of human anomalies contained by
the Foundation, it’s not a stretch to say

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.060
that they most likely wish they were ordinary,
like anyone else.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:32.820
That they didn’t have to be locked up in
a containment cell for the rest of their lives.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.649
As the years have gone by, the Foundation,
much like any organization, has changed a

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:38.649
lot.

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:43.030
More facilities have pushed for ethical and
humane treatment of anomalies, some going

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:47.670
so far as to integrate safe anomalies into
the command structure of the organization

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:48.670
itself.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:52.559
With groups such as the Ethics Committee keeping
the Foundation’s most hardline normalcy

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:58.040
supremacists from mistreating or mishandling
the objects they’re supposed to contain,

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:02.719
it’s hard to imagine that anything would
slip by the ever-watchful eye of the Foundation’s

00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:09.010
surveillance network, but in an organization
this large, incidents are still bound to happen.

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:14.540
While anomalies can be dangerous, the Foundation
as a whole backs the ideal that they should

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.630
be given ethical treatment, at least as much
as they can afford.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:23.140
For safer, less dangerous anomalies, this
is a lot easier to enforce.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:28.369
To suggest rehabilitation efforts and recreational
privileges to be given to an anomaly capable

00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:33.690
of ending human life at a moment’s notice
raises a lot more eyebrows, even in the most

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.700
progressive sects of the Foundation.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.909
That line becomes blurred when dealing with
intelligent entities.

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:42.900
What defines intelligence?

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.130
Sapience?

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:49.460
What distinguishes SCP-682, the indestructible
lizard with a massive disgust for all life

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:56.659
from SCP-239, an ultimately innocent little
girl with world-breaking reality-bending powers?

00:01:56.659 --> 00:02:00.829
This is the sort of argument that divides
the upper ranks of the Foundation.

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:06.530
Is the integration of these anomalies the
answer, or should they be sealed away forever?

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:11.730
Should they be uniformly treated as monsters
and freaks, unfit to ever leave their cells

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.180
aside from being used in testing?

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:18.930
Fortunately for the anomaly rights activists
in the crowd, the modern Foundation is much

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:25.279
more lenient than it had been in decades past,
as research has proven that even dangerous

00:02:25.279 --> 00:02:31.139
anomalies, when given friendly treatment and
basic rights, are more compliant, happy, and

00:02:31.139 --> 00:02:32.930
feel less strife about their situation.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:36.639
They can even be useful in some situations.

00:02:36.639 --> 00:02:44.090
Take SCP-5595, a sentient, sarcastic Gumball
machine located at Site-322 whose affinity

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:49.959
for mathematics and harmless nature earned
it a position at the site’s accounting department,

00:02:49.959 --> 00:02:54.609
as part of a larger Foundation initiative
called the Integration Program, which focused

00:02:54.609 --> 00:02:58.180
on integrating harmless anomalies into the
Site itself.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:04.489
In fact, SCP-5595’s accounting skills were
so great that it reduced Site-322’s spending

00:03:04.489 --> 00:03:10.620
costs overall and opened the higher-ups to
the idea of integrating more anomalies across

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.030
the organization.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:17.629
If you need another example, SCP-999, the
adorable orange blob lovingly nicknamed the

00:03:17.629 --> 00:03:22.739
“Tickle Monster”, has been used as a therapy
object at Site-19 for years!

00:03:22.739 --> 00:03:27.829
But there is one side of the debate that spurs
more controversy than any other.

00:03:27.829 --> 00:03:30.109
Using anomalies as living weapons.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:35.199
The Foundation has long abided by the directive
that its objects are to be contained and studied

00:03:35.199 --> 00:03:40.719
instead of used in the field, as an uncontrollable
object is more dangerous outside of a cell

00:03:40.719 --> 00:03:41.719
than in.

00:03:41.719 --> 00:03:45.909
But that directive has changed, especially
in recent times.

00:03:45.909 --> 00:03:50.889
The Chaos Insurgency, one of the Foundation’s
greatest foes, utilizes anomalies as weapons

00:03:50.889 --> 00:03:54.819
to achieve their goals, as do many other groups
of interest.

00:03:54.819 --> 00:03:58.379
When trained human soldiers just aren’t
enough to contend with all of the enemies

00:03:58.379 --> 00:04:02.709
the Foundation deals with, it's no wonder
they began to explore other options.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:06.769
And that brings us to the subject of today’s
video.

00:04:06.769 --> 00:04:13.779
The tale of SCP-4793, an anomaly trained as
a brutalizing soldier who never really wanted

00:04:13.779 --> 00:04:15.099
to fight.

00:04:15.099 --> 00:04:20.939
This is the story of Androcles, a warrior
with a blazing, savage fury in his body, but

00:04:20.939 --> 00:04:24.050
with a gentle, tender longing in his heart.

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:28.210
It all started during a Foundation raid on
a Chaos Insurgency operation located in a

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:31.169
mountain cave in the southern region of Greece.

00:04:31.169 --> 00:04:35.990
The deadly insurgency, always on the prowl
for more anomalous weapons to use in its unending

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:40.750
battle against the Foundation, had hired a
team of mercenaries to scour the region for

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:43.170
potential anomalous activity.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:47.741
They came across something buried in the mountains
they were certain was anomalous, and after

00:04:47.741 --> 00:04:52.819
communicating with their superiors, decided
to dig it up and see what it was about.

00:04:52.819 --> 00:04:57.340
Naturally, word of such a discovery travels
fast, and with how many undercover operatives

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:02.310
the Foundation keeps embedded inside the Insurgency
in order to keep tabs on what their enemies

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:07.820
are doing, it's no surprise that the Foundation
mobilized its forces to get the drop on whatever

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:10.880
this anomalous excavation site was.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.729
The mission was simple enough.

00:05:12.729 --> 00:05:18.639
MTF Upsilon-11, nicknamed “Avalon’s Wake”,
a team of combat specialists led by the skilled

00:05:18.639 --> 00:05:24.219
Captain Holly Shore, would infiltrate their
camp and seize any anomalous objects in the

00:05:24.219 --> 00:05:25.360
mercenaries' possession.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:29.819
Getting past the relatively unguarded entrance
was a cake walk, as the task force took out

00:05:29.819 --> 00:05:34.210
a single guard and were able to slip deeper
into the cave undetected.

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:40.610
Inside, they found a massive pit, surrounded
by colorful stalagmites and flowing waterfalls.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:45.449
At the center of the pit, next to a smattering
of camping supplies and bright floodlights,

00:05:45.449 --> 00:05:50.509
was a large stone stele, a type of pillar
most often used in ancient times that would

00:05:50.509 --> 00:05:53.840
be carved with important messages or stories.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:58.249
The details were grainy from a distance, but
the team could make out an engraved image

00:05:58.249 --> 00:06:01.410
of a Spartan Hoplite soldier on the pillar.

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:05.499
Surrounding the stele were five mercenaries,
armed and in the process of digging out the

00:06:05.499 --> 00:06:07.639
pillar from beneath the rock.

00:06:07.639 --> 00:06:13.110
Captain Shore knew that this was most likely
the big object the Chaos Insurgency were after.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:17.539
She and her team took cover, waiting for the
opportune moment to strike, but their wait

00:06:17.539 --> 00:06:19.300
wasn’t long.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:22.370
One of the mercenaries shoveling the ground
near the stele let out a scream.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:26.840
They had cut themselves, splattering a small
amount of blood on the stone monument.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:29.240
The mercenaries panicked, readying their arms.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:33.910
They weren’t sure what was going to happen
next, but with enough experience in the field,

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:39.499
they knew that introducing an anomaly to human
blood often had severe consequences.

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:42.379
And their suspicions were proven correct.

00:06:42.379 --> 00:06:47.190
A flash of light surrounded the cave, and
from the stele emerged a warrior, clad in

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:51.379
the same armor as the Spartan soldier engraved
on the monument’s carving.

00:06:51.379 --> 00:06:56.600
The entity was clearly confused, and asked,
in English, if the mercenaries spoke greek.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:00.860
Instead, they thrust their guns forward, screaming
at the soldier to not move.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:05.240
The soldier was compliant, but one of the
mercenaries, feeling it to be a cruel way

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:10.719
to establish dominance over their new anomalous
toy, shot at the soldier’s exposed leg.

00:07:10.719 --> 00:07:14.759
What happened next was a whirlwind of swearing,
blood, and combat.

00:07:14.759 --> 00:07:19.729
The mercenaries opened fire on the soldier,
who retaliated back by using powerful hand-to-hand

00:07:19.729 --> 00:07:20.729
combat.

00:07:20.729 --> 00:07:24.289
For whatever reason, bullets just couldn’t
seem to harm the soldier.

00:07:24.289 --> 00:07:29.110
He tanked dozens of open shots across his
body, the rounds deflecting off of his armor.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:33.340
As the soldier picked up a mercenary by the
throat, the kevlar vest he was wearing suddenly

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:38.759
flung itself from the man’s body and integrated
itself onto the soldier’s armor.

00:07:38.759 --> 00:07:42.979
The mercenary immediately recognized this
as one of the soldier’s anomalous abilities

00:07:42.979 --> 00:07:48.330
but was powerless to stop it as he was slammed
against the stone wall, falling to the ground.

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:53.070
The Foundation task force watched in awe as
the soldier took out each of the mercenaries,

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:54.340
one by one.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:58.020
Captain Shore, seeing that the soldier was
continually begging the mercenaries to stop

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:03.400
shooting at it the entire time, sensed that
there was a peaceful, humane side to the entity,

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:08.360
a stark contrast to the acts of brutality
it used to dispatch the mercenaries.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:11.879
Shore told her men to move forward, but with
their weapons lowered.

00:08:11.879 --> 00:08:16.529
The soldier, holding onto a knife it grabbed
earlier, stood on guard, but surrendered without

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:20.789
question when he realized the Foundation operatives
were not there to fight him.

00:08:20.789 --> 00:08:25.250
Captain Shore introduced herself and her men
as a part of the Foundation, and the soldier,

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:30.770
clearly upset and distraught over the carnage
he caused, introduced himself as Androcles.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:34.949
The team promised Androcles they would take
him somewhere safe, and he complied.

00:08:34.949 --> 00:08:40.020
Little would he know that his journey with
the Foundation was just beginning.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:46.459
Androcles was given the designation SCP-4793,
and initial assessment found him to be anomalously

00:08:46.459 --> 00:08:51.279
strong, with the ability to integrate any
solid material into a weapon, either as a

00:08:51.279 --> 00:08:56.630
piece of armor, like it did with the mercenaries’
kevlar vest, or as a weapon itself, such as

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:00.090
turning the steel leg of a chair into a sharpened
sword.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:05.130
Though this ability did have its limits, as
Androcles had difficulty incorporating firearms

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:08.339
and complex electronics as weapons or armor.

00:09:08.339 --> 00:09:15.110
On top of that, SCP-4793 was extremely durable
and able to heal any wounds on its body almost

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:16.950
instantaneously.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:22.740
Coupled with his highly trained fighting skills
and raging fury, Androcles was a true warrior,

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.079
capable of great power and might.

00:09:25.079 --> 00:09:29.380
But his wild side seemed to disappear when
the heat of battle died down.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:33.920
One of Site-20’s senior researchers, Dr.
Fitz-Patrick was tasked with interviewing

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:41.620
SCP-4793 weekly, and she discovered that SCP-4793
had a completely different element to his

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:42.620
personality.

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:47.290
He was intelligent, kind, gentle, and hated
fighting.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:51.339
He couldn’t remember much of his life from
thousands of years ago, but he knew that he

00:09:51.339 --> 00:09:56.660
was a great warrior who caused mass destruction
with his power alone.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:58.350
Androcles didn’t want to be someone like
that.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:04.160
He had an interest in history, in books, and
learning why he woke up, what the world was

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:07.209
like now, and why it had changed.

00:10:07.209 --> 00:10:11.310
Androcles wanted to know why there were metal
birds in the sky and horseless chariots on

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:12.310
the ground.

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:18.589
Dr. Fitz-Patrick found him to be a remarkable
person and commended SCP-4793’s behavior

00:10:18.589 --> 00:10:23.630
with access to various literature and history
books so he could learn about the things he

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:25.520
desperately wanted to know.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:31.400
But most of all, she was taken back by how
averse he was to becoming his past self, a

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.529
heartless warrior who killed indiscriminately.

00:10:33.529 --> 00:10:39.089
It seemed as if Androcles was so traumatized
by his past actions that he sealed away those

00:10:39.089 --> 00:10:42.180
memories to forget about them as best he could.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:47.209
But Site-20’s director, Jack Hargraves,
saw Androcles as a mere tool.

00:10:47.209 --> 00:10:51.899
Something he could use to achieve a nefarious
goal he had been planning for a long, long

00:10:51.899 --> 00:10:53.850
time.

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:58.209
Hargraves wanted to use SCP-4793’s raw power
to benefit the Foundation.

00:10:58.209 --> 00:11:03.860
From his office, he sat back, imagining the
unstoppable force that a trained Androcles

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:04.910
would be.

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:09.509
If he could force him to fight, and he knew
he could, then the Foundation would have a

00:11:09.509 --> 00:11:12.150
deadly weapon in their hands.

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:16.480
Something that would surely even the odds
between the Chaos Insurgency and those other

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.800
pesky groups of interest.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:24.180
Director Hargraves forced SCP-4793 to train
his combat abilities in a variety of sparring

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:29.210
sessions with Captain Shore, the task force
captain who discovered him in the mountains.

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:33.950
Hargraves’ regimen was brutal, and he often
threatened to blow up the explosive collars

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:41.100
on SCP-4793’s neck and wrists if he held
back against Shore or disobeyed his orders.

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:46.570
Androcles could take the explosion, but Shore
would surely be caught in the blast, killing

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:47.570
her.

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:52.339
Androcles hated Hargraves, but cared about
Shore, who showed him kindness and understood

00:11:52.339 --> 00:11:54.130
his difficult position.

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:58.010
Over the next two years, Androcles would train
weekly with Shore, sparring with each other

00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:02.459
using a variety of weapons, from swords to
firearms.

00:12:02.459 --> 00:12:08.949
SCP-4793 still held back, not wanting to fight,
and wanting even less to accidentally injure

00:12:08.949 --> 00:12:12.550
Holly Shore, who he was growing to see as
a friend.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:18.440
In the meantime, Dr. Fitz-Patrick continued
to interview SCP-4793 weekly, also growing

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:20.430
a friendship with the entity.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:24.640
But for as much as she cared about Androcles,
she couldn’t help him the way she wanted

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:25.750
to.

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:31.450
Hargraves was set on making SCP-4793 a functional
weapon on the field, and he was growing impatient

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:33.360
waiting for results.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:37.500
Hargraves was pushing Androcles beyond his
comfort zone, switching up his sparring partners

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:42.820
from Shore, who he trusted deeply, to other
individuals, or changing what weapons he had

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:44.380
to use.

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:49.279
Androcles hated this, not because he was scared
to fight, but because he was anxious about

00:12:49.279 --> 00:12:52.389
what he could become if he let loose.

00:12:52.389 --> 00:12:55.949
He never wanted to be the monster that he
knew he was capable of being.

00:12:55.949 --> 00:12:58.620
He never wanted to hurt someone.

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:02.240
In the meantime, Hargraves began to have doubts
about Androcles.

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:06.899
His humanity and reluctance would slow him
down in the field, keep him from being the

00:13:06.899 --> 00:13:10.110
perfect super-soldier Hargraves wanted him
to be.

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:15.589
So he began development on another project,
codenamed X06.

00:13:15.589 --> 00:13:20.470
This mysterious weapons program was kept under
wraps, limited in knowledge to only Hargraves

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:22.720
and his most trusted men.

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:27.029
If he couldn’t have Androcles, he would
simply have to do better.

00:13:27.029 --> 00:13:28.449
And he knew he would.

00:13:28.449 --> 00:13:33.889
While Hargraves worked in the shadows, the
SCP-4793 research team uncovered a section

00:13:33.889 --> 00:13:36.420
of Androcles’ past that he had forgotten.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:41.810
The stele he was trapped inside had an inscription
on its front, written in ancient greek.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:46.860
When it was translated and sent to Dr. Fitz-Patrick,
this is what it read.

00:13:46.860 --> 00:13:52.449
Gather around me, children, I will tell you
the story of sweet Androcles.

00:13:52.449 --> 00:13:58.940
Fierce as a pride of lions and as cunning
as a pack of wolves, he lived for nothing

00:13:58.940 --> 00:13:59.940
but battle.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:05.060
He was beloved by his countrymen and feared
by his enemies, so much so that Ares Himself

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:09.399
strode down from Olympus to challenge him
to single combat.

00:14:09.399 --> 00:14:14.430
For ten days they fought a terrible Duel,
their blades cutting earth into islands and

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:17.820
the sparks turning mountains into forges for
Hephaestus.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:23.329
Impressed, he granted Androcles a boon: So
long as he fought, he would never know defeat

00:14:23.329 --> 00:14:30.579
or age and by mixing his Ichor with Androcles'
blood, Ares declared him kin to the Gods themselves.

00:14:30.579 --> 00:14:35.370
As he came to bear on the world, he met his
match in a woman from a distant land.

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:40.690
With skin of whitest sand, covered in blues
from the ocean, she blazed in his eyes like

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:42.000
Helios' chariot.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.949
Together, the mountains bowed before them.

00:14:44.949 --> 00:14:50.720
But even as Eros' arrow brought them together,
an arrow split them apart, for Jealous Ares

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:54.790
saw his favored love something other than
Himself.

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:59.390
With his guiding star gone, Androcles tore
the bones of the Earth itself.

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:05.670
With his rage and lust for battle extinguished,
he turned the battlefield into Twin mountains.

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:10.180
With his purpose lost, he entombed them forevermore.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:13.320
Androcles was shaken by the revelations of
his warrior past.

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:17.480
And in the present, he couldn’t shake the
feeling that Captain Shore reminded him of

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:18.700
his past lover.

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:24.240
The feeling was so strong, that during a sparring
session, Androcles passed out, overwhelmed

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:31.290
by how much she reminded him of her, the woman
who he remembered to be his wife, Arabel.

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:35.839
Androcles continued to confide in Dr. Fitz-Patrick
about his feelings about Captain Shore, and

00:15:35.839 --> 00:15:37.720
especially about fighting for the Foundation.

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:43.170
He didn’t understand this strange, new world,
or what exactly he would be fighting for.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:48.350
And the stories he heard about previous attempts
to utilize anomalous soldiers in battle terrified

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:49.350
him.

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:55.399
The story of SCP-076, Able, killing his entire
Task Force team after losing control haunted

00:15:55.399 --> 00:15:56.480
him at night.

00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:59.139
He never wanted to become that.

00:15:59.139 --> 00:16:03.709
But Hargraves’ secret project reached its
completion before Androcles could be molded

00:16:03.709 --> 00:16:05.230
into the perfect warrior.

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:06.431
To celebrate the creation of what he told
Dr. Fitz-Patrick was the perfect warrior,

00:16:06.431 --> 00:16:08.540
he invited her to be assigned to Project-X09.
Little did Hargraves know, however, that Fitz-Patrick

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:14.140
was keeping tabs on all of his shady behavior,
in hopes of one day exposing him for the monster

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:18.620
that he was to the Ethics Committee, or maybe
even the Overseer Council.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:23.889
Still, she took the job, wanting to see what
monstrosity Hargraves had created as a result

00:16:23.889 --> 00:16:25.550
of his experiments.

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:27.890
Fitz-Patrick was shocked to see it.

00:16:27.890 --> 00:16:33.000
Hargraves’ secret experiment was a black,
winged, clawed creature with way too many

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:34.150
teeth.

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:40.000
From behind its containment cylinder, it grinned
and chuckled an inhuman laugh.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.410
Hargraves was truly creating monsters.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:47.470
As Hargraves explained, the creature had near-human
intelligence and could reproduce asexually,

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:50.970
meaning all it took was one of them for it
to multiply.

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:56.190
With this new anomaly, he could revolutionize
the Foundation’s ways of waging war.

00:16:56.190 --> 00:17:01.420
A perfect soldier, one that wouldn’t be
held back by human emotion.

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:05.640
Fitz-Patrick voiced her concern but was cut
short by Hargraves suddenly panicking.

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:10.960
He noticed that there was only one X06 entity
in the cylinder, when he was sure there were

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:11.960
two.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:15.950
And suddenly, from the ceiling, one of the
entities fell to the ground, flapping its

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:18.700
wings and screaming in the researcher's faces.

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:20.760
The worst had happened.

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:25.600
The X06 entities had broken free, and if they
weren’t stopped soon, they would run rampant

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.010
over Site-20.

00:17:27.010 --> 00:17:31.230
The two fled for safety, but the horrifying
creature chased after them.

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:34.540
Androcles and Captain Shore soon learned of
the containment breach as well, after their

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:38.600
sparring session was cut short by a creature
breaking into the room.

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:41.520
Androcles made short work of it, but it was
too late.

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:44.420
Site-20 was overrun with Hargraves’ beasts.

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:49.270
There were hundreds of them, and those numbers
would continue to grow.

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:54.430
They infiltrated the entire facility, leaving
Androcles and Captain Shore with one option:

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:56.010
to fight.

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:59.290
Androcles didn’t want to do it, but this
was different.

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:03.960
He needed to be a hero and save the people
still trapped in Site-20’s facilities.

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:09.480
He would have to use force, but if he was
helping others, then it was justified, he

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:10.850
reluctantly told himself.

00:18:10.850 --> 00:18:12.320
Still, he hated it.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:18.660
And as Captain Shore and her task force, as
well as SCP-4793, moved through Site-20, taking

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:24.070
out one entity after another, Androcles realized
how hopeless the situation was looking.

00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:26.290
There were simply too many of them.

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:30.220
They needed to focus their efforts on getting
people out of the site rather than hoping

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:31.220
to fight back.

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:35.870
While most personnel were slaughtered in the
carnage, at the Site’s D-Class block, the

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:41.260
team found a holdout of guards and D-class,
who were conveniently relocated to an above-ground

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:45.060
elevator that could escort them safely out
of the site.

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:49.220
Androcles made the decision there, to let
Captain Shore and her men, as well as the

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:53.240
survivors, get to the surface, while he would
stay below and fight.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:56.620
He didn’t want to do it, but Androcles had
a plan.

00:18:56.620 --> 00:19:00.690
Shore didn’t want to leave him behind, but
she had no choice.

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:05.570
After parting in the heat of an X06 ambush
on the block, Androcles was alone, while the

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:07.960
survivors were on the surface.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:12.810
Fighting without holding back, Androcles tore
through hundreds of X06 entities, going deeper

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:14.760
and deeper into the site.

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:20.920
His plan was dangerous, but it would save
everyone, at the expense of his own life.

00:19:20.920 --> 00:19:26.210
Androcles knew how dangerous those X06 entities
could be if they were let loose into the world,

00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:31.850
and that was why he decided he would blow
up Site-20’s reactor, destroying both himself,

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:34.520
the site, and every single creature.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:38.970
As he was about to do just that, Androcles
found Director Hargraves’ in the rubble

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:40.790
of the reactor room.

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:45.200
Hargrave was heavily wounded, and Androcles
felt such rage and anger towards the man,

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:49.640
especially when he revealed that the X06 creatures
were genetically engineered from Androcles’

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:50.640
own blood.

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:52.640
But he didn’t hurt him.

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:56.110
He was better than the monster Hargrave saw
him as.

00:19:56.110 --> 00:20:00.440
Instead, Androcles sent Hargraves up on the
elevator to the surface, knowing that the

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:05.520
Overseer Council would serve a far worse punishment
than he ever could.

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:08.800
Before blowing up the reactor, Androcles recorded
one last message, using equipment that was

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:09.800
attached to his task force helmet.

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:13.800
He addressed it to Holly Shore, the captain
who had shown him so much kindness.

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:17.850
“I was born to a farmer and grew into a
warrior.

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:20.510
I battled Ares to a standstill.

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:22.230
I won wars singlehandedly.

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:24.380
Then I met my wife.

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:30.850
We were set to claim the world, two immortals
who wanted to bring a chaotic world some semblance

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:31.850
of peace.

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:33.540
And then Ares killed her.

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:37.390
And I lost everything.

00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:38.970
And now I'm here.

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:39.970
Alone.

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:40.970
Adrift.

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:43.990
A stranger surrounded by even stranger things.

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:48.110
But within you, I see the spark I saw in her.

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:51.460
A burning desire to make the world better.

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:54.510
It makes me want to be better.

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:58.640
And I don't know if you feel the same, or
whether I'll get out of here…

00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:02.020
But I will fight for you.

00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:04.250
Die if I have to.

00:21:04.250 --> 00:21:05.580
I love you.”

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:11.630
And with that, Androcles, one of the greatest
warriors the Foundation had ever known, sacrificed

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:18.130
his life to blow up Site-20’s nuclear reactor,
destroying the facility and saving the world

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:20.400
from Hargrave’s deadly creatures.

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:25.670
To those who knew him, especially Captain
Shore, he will never be forgotten - Because

00:21:25.670 --> 00:21:28.340
true heroes never really die.

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:32.440
Now go check out “What Actually Happened
to Major Alexei Belitrov?

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:38.960
SCP-2273 - Tale” and “SCP-507 - Reluctant
Dimension Hopper” for more journeys into

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:42.850
the lives and minds of the Foundation’s
more sympathetic prisoners!

